All firmware, Home Assistant configuration and tools were written for this project. The RF protocol
facts (frame layout, timing, key codes, toggle bit, hold behaviour) come from the author's own captures
of the Ciarko Duo 74 remote (Broadlink, RTL-SDR / rtl_433 and the ESP receiver) and were cross-checked
against the following MIT-licensed project, which is gratefully acknowledged:

- ciarko-hood-433-esphome - Copyright (c) 2026 Adam Węglarz - MIT
  https://github.com/AdamWeglarz/ciarko-hood-433-esphome
  (ideas: flip the toggle bit on every transmitted press, send the whole burst back to back in one
  transmit buffer; codes of the XY8011-RF remote of a Ciarko SU Mini used to confirm that the key codes
  are shared between remotes)

The untested hood profiles (esphome/profiles/elica_came18, novy_840029, luxair_came18, zephyr_pt2262_315) were
written from published protocol facts and captures, gratefully acknowledged:

- UberGuidoZ/Flipper – Flipper Zero Sub-GHz captures (Cooker_Hoods/Elica, Misc/Novy_Pure_Line_682X_Kitchen_Hood)
  https://github.com/UberGuidoZ/Flipper
- elica-rangehood-matter - Crystal-Matter - MIT – Elica captures
  https://github.com/Crystal-Matter/elica-rangehood-matter
- novy-esphome - VanIseghemThomas – Novy codes and timing
  https://github.com/VanIseghemThomas/novy-esphome
- esp-home-hob2hood-luxair - josephdouce – Luxair raw timings
  https://github.com/josephdouce/esp-home-hob2hood-luxair
